$CATEGORY: Q11 - Loops and strings

::Q11_01::
loop - A statement that executes a sequence of statements repeatedly.{TRUE}

::Q11_02::
loop body - The statements inside the loop normally limited by square braquets {FALSE#Curly braquets}

::Q11_03::
infinite loop - A loop whose condition is always true.{TRUE}

::Q11_04::
index - {
    ~A variable that is initialized, tested, and updated in order to control a loop.
    =An integer variable or value used to indicate a character in a string.
}

::Q11_05::
loop variable - {
    =A variable that is initialized, tested, and updated in order to control a loop.
    ~An integer variable or value used to indicate a character in a string.
}

::Q11_06::
iteration - Execution of the loop body for a particular value of the loop variable.{TRUE}

::Q11_07::
Unicode - An international standard for representing characters in most of the languages.{TRUE}

::Q11_08::
empty string - The string which contains no characters and has a length of zero.{TRUE}

$CATEGORY: Q12 - String functions

Given the string s initialized to the value "banana", explain the functionality of

::Q12_01::
s.length() {}

::Q12_02::
s.charAt(0) {}

::Q12_03a::
s.indexOf('a') {}

::Q12_03b::
s.indexOf('a', 1) {}

::Q12_04a::
s.substring(0, 3) {}

::Q12_04b::
s.substring(2) {}

::Q12_05::
s.compareTo("banner"){}

::Q12_06::
s.equals("orange") {}